{
  "$comment": "Foreground/background token pairs rated by scripts/check-contrast.mjs (WCAG 2.1). kind: text >= 4.5, large >= 3 (24px, or 18.66px bold), ui >= 3 (focus rings, borders, icons that carry state). tokens.file is the one token source; tokens.themes maps each theme to the CSS blocks read for it, in order, later blocks overriding earlier ones (a block inside an at-rule is named by its path, e.g. \"@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) :root\"); two themes may not read the same blocks, and a block no theme reads may not define a token the pairs use. Nested style rules are refused. A translucent bg needs \"over\", the opaque token it sits on; a translucent fg is composited onto the bg. \"gate\": false keeps a pair's reading in the output without failing the run; it needs a \"why\" citing an issue (#n), every theme keeps at least one gated pair, and an exempt pair that meets its threshold fails the run until the exemption is removed. The exempt pairs fail on today's canvas values and are open questions for #18. Pairs come from the canvas boards Tokens, Foundations, Placement, Components and Motion and states. Not listed on purpose: --tertiary, --separator and --hairline (dividers and chevrons, decorative, never text), locked points (rgba white 28%, inactive), --lit-deep and --atmosphere (glow only).",
  "tokens": {
    "file": "design/tokens.css",
    "themes": {
      "light": [":root"],
      "dark": [":root", "[data-theme=\"dark\"]"]
    }
  },
